      "problemStatement": "用 Taylor 展开计算下列极限：\n(1) $\\\\lim_{x\\\\to 0}\\\\dfrac{\\\\cos x-e^{-x^2/2}}{x^4}$；\n(2) $\\\\lim_{x\\\\to 0}\\\\dfrac{\\\\arcsin x-\\\\sin x}{x^3}$。",
      "solution": "(1) $\\\\cos x=1-\\\\frac{x^2}{2}+\\\\frac{x^4}{24}+O(x^6)$，$e^{-x^2/2}=1-\\\\frac{x^2}{2}+\\\\frac{x^4}{8}+O(x^6)$（代入 $t=-x^2/2$ 到 $e^t=1+t+t^2/2+\\\\cdots$）。\n$\\\\cos x-e^{-x^2/2}=\\\\frac{x^4}{24}-\\\\frac{x^4}{8}+O(x^6)=x^4\\\\left(\\\\frac{1}{24}-\\\\frac{1}{8}\\\\right)+O(x^6)=-\\\\frac{x^4}{12}+O(x^6)$。\n故极限 $=-\\\\dfrac{1}{12}$。\n(2) $\\\\arcsin x=x+\\\\frac{x^3}{6}+O(x^5)$，$\\\\sin x=x-\\\\frac{x^3}{6}+O(x^5)$。\n$\\\\arcsin x-\\\\sin x=\\\\frac{x^3}{6}+\\\\frac{x^3}{6}+O(x^5)=\\\\frac{x^3}{3}+O(x^5)$。\n故极限 $=\\\\dfrac{1}{3}$。",
